# macOS
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Jupyter / IDE
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/

# Virtual environment
/.venv

# Data: large third-party rasters + generated aligned outputs (input_data/cleaned_aligned).
# Not for GitHub -- obtain/regenerate locally.
/input_data

# Optimization outputs (03) + figures (04): generated, regenerate locally.
/output_data
/figures

# R: user-global ~/.R/Makevars holds the macOS toolchain fixes (not in-repo).
gurobi.log
.Rhistory
.RData
Rplots.pdf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED DATA, ANYWHERE (2026-09-15). Rasters, images, decks, binary arrays and vector outputs
# are regenerable from the notebooks and never belong on GitHub, whatever folder they land in --
# the old per-folder rules missed a 54 MB `_superseded_*` block and the Alberta `analysis/` tree.
# The few deliberate exceptions are re-included BY NAME at the bottom of this file.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tif
*.tiff
*.vrt
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.npz
*.npy
*.parquet
*.feather
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.rds
*.gpkg
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg

# Flagship analyses (analyses/<name>/): notebooks, the spec (the pre-registration: frozen
# manifests + sha256, scenarios, the living methods/results logs) and the SMALL frozen audit
# records (feature_characterization.csv, audit_constants.json, the northern H7 sign-off) are
# TRACKED -- they are the record. Everything generated and regenerable is not: the bulky curve
# archive (hash-pinned by audit_constants.json), the feature-card PDFs, figures, the per-cell
# solution matrices (runs/), the Alberta analysis outputs (analysis/ -- rasters, cluster vectors
# and result tables from 08/11), and the per-notebook execution logs written by run_v31.sh.
analyses/*/figures/
analyses/*/audit/feature_cards/
analyses/*/audit/feature_cards_ab/
analyses/*/audit/audit_objects/feature_audit.npz
analyses/*/audit/audit_objects_ab/feature_audit.npz
analyses/*/runs/
analyses/*/runs_*/
analyses/*/analysis/
analyses/*/logs/

# Alberta prioritization acquired layers (analyses/alberta_prioritization/data/): the raw downloads
# (multi-GB: GVI FGDB, ACI GeoTIFF, SRP zips, REST pulls) are NOT tracked -- data/README.md,
# data/acquire.py and data/provenance.json (URL + sha256 per file) are the record; re-acquire locally.
# The small derived extent polygon (data/ab_extent_v1.gpkg) stays tracked (re-included below).
analyses/*/data/tenure/
analyses/*/data/aoi/
analyses/*/data/pa/
analyses/*/data/derived/

# Director packages (analyses/*/director_package/): EVERYTHING inside is generated by 19/20/21
# (y2y) or 12/13 (Alberta) -- geotiffs, figures, the curated director_outputs, the CSV tables,
# cluster vectors, decks, dev _smoke/ runs and any _superseded_* block kept on disk for reference.
# Only the two small human-readable indexes stay tracked, so a commit still says what the package
# contained; the tables themselves are re-derived by re-running 19 (y2y) / 12 (Alberta).
analyses/*/director_package/**
!analyses/*/director_package/deck_outline.md
!analyses/*/director_package/summary.json

# Tracked on purpose (NOT ignored): config.py, *.py, *.R, *.ipynb, requirements.txt,
# requirements-R.txt, CLAUDE.md, .claude/settings.json, docs/, configs/ (frozen run configs),
# archive/ (frozen v1 notebooks; their outputs live in gitignored output_data/),
# analyses/*/spec/ (study plans, frozen manifests + sha256, methods/results logs),
# analyses/*/audit/audit_objects*/{feature_characterization.csv,audit_constants.json}.
# NOTE: a global rule above (e.g. *.png) also blocks a future intentional image under docs/ --
# re-include it by name here rather than `git add -f`, so the exception is visible.

# Deliberate exceptions to the global data rules, re-included by name:
#  - the small derived Alberta extent polygon = the record of the study extent
#  - the northern-connectivity H7 human sign-off: node_parts.gpkg beside node_parts.csv +
#    multipart_review.csv (corridors_core._H7_FILES expects all three git-tracked)
!analyses/alberta_prioritization/data/ab_extent_v1.gpkg
!analyses/northern_connectivity/audit/audit_objects/node_parts.gpkg
